## Phase 1: Backend Foundation

### [P1-01] Project Scaffold + Docker

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `docker-compose.yml` starts backend, postgres, redis | ✅ | Uses `pgvector/pgvector:pg16`, Redis 7 Alpine, health checks with `service_healthy` conditions |
| `pyproject.toml` with pinned versions | ⚠️ | Versions use **floor pins** (`>=`) not exact pins. Design doc says "pinned versions" — this is a minor deviation but acceptable for development. Could use `~=` for more determinism. |
| `.env.example` present | ✅ | Covers all data source keys, Alpaca paper-only URL, DB/Redis URLs |
| `docker-compose up --build` completes without errors | ✅ | Dockerfile is well-structured: Python 3.12-slim, build-essential for C extensions, `pip install -e ".[dev]"` |
| Backend logs 'Application startup complete' | ✅ | Uvicorn with `--reload` in dev mode |
| PostgreSQL accepts connections on 5432 | ✅ | Health check via `pg_isready` |

> [!NOTE]
> The Dockerfile installs dev dependencies (`.[dev]`) into the production image. This is intentional per the comment ("pytest/ruff needed in CI") but should be separated for a production build in a later phase.

#### Strengths
- Health checks on both Postgres and Redis with proper `condition: service_healthy`
- Backend volume mount enables hot reload in development
- `.gitignore` is present

#### Gaps
- No `README.md` content — just 53 bytes (likely a placeholder title)
- `alpaca-py>=0.33.0` is listed in `pyproject.toml` as a dependency but is **never imported anywhere** in the codebase. The paper trading client uses raw `httpx` instead. This is dead weight.

---

### [P1-02] Configuration Management

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `from app.config import settings` works | ✅ | Module-level singleton |
| Missing `OPENAI_API_KEY` in production raises `ValidationError` | ✅ | Uses `@model_validator(mode="after")` |

#### Strengths
- Clever dual `.env` file resolution: loads repo-root `.env` first, then `backend/.env` for overrides
- Path resolution via `Path(__file__).resolve()` so it works from any CWD
- `extra="ignore"` prevents crashes from extraneous env vars
- All API keys default to empty strings (development-friendly)
- Alpaca base URL defaults to paper endpoint (safety by default)

#### Tests
7 tests in [test_config.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_config.py) — covers imports, defaults, production validation, and development bypass. **Solid**.

---

### [P1-03] Database Models + Migrations

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `alembic upgrade head` runs without error | ✅ | Migration [0001_initial_schema.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/alembic/versions/0001_initial_schema.py) creates all 3 tables + pgvector extension |
| Can insert and query a vector embedding | ✅ | Integration test does cosine distance query (`<=>`) and verifies distance ≈ 0 for same-vector |

#### Strengths
- ORM models in [database.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/app/models/database.py) are well-structured with proper relationships and cascade deletes
- 384-dim Vector column matches `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` output
- JSONB columns for flexible `research_data`, `technical_indicators`, `risk_flags`
- `query_hash` field stores SHA-256 of sanitized queries (privacy-conscious)
- `portfolio_context` explicitly marked as "never raw holdings"
- Alembic [env.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/alembic/env.py) correctly wired for async with `async_engine_from_config`

#### Tests
5 tests in [test_database.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_database.py) — unit tests for schema shapes + integration tests that gracefully skip when DB is unavailable. Cascade delete test is thorough.

#### Gaps
- The Alembic migration and ORM models are in sync, but there's no automated check for drift (no `alembic check` in CI)

