## Phase 2: Data Integration Layer

### [P2-01] SEC EDGAR Client

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `get_company_filings('AAPL')` returns 10+ filings | ✅ | Test provides 12 mock filings, asserts ≥10 |
| Rate limiting respects SEC 10 req/sec | ✅ | Custom `_TokenBucket` with async lock; tested that 11 sequential acquires take ≥0.05s |
| Handles 404 for invalid CIK | ✅ | Raises `CIKNotFoundError` |

#### Strengths
- Full implementation of all 3 specified functions plus a bonus `get_institutional_holdings()` for 13F filings
- Proper ticker→CIK resolution via SEC's `company_tickers.json` with caching
- Token bucket rate limiter is well-engineered: SMA-seeded, async-safe, with test helpers
- User-Agent header set from config on every request (SEC fair-access compliance)
- Custom exception hierarchy: `SECEdgarError` → `CIKNotFoundError`, `RateLimitError`
- XBRL financial facts parsed with proper concept/unit/period handling

#### Tests
15 tests in [test_sec_edgar.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_sec_edgar.py) — all using `httpx.MockTransport` (no live calls). Coverage includes ticker resolution, caching, form filtering, limit, 404 handling, rate limiter, UA header, and JSON round-tripping. **Excellent test quality**.

#### Design Doc Conformance
- `get_company_filings(ticker)` → `list[Filing]` ✅
- `get_financial_statements(cik, form_type)` → `FinancialData` ✅
- `get_insider_trades(ticker)` → `list[InsiderTrade]` ✅

