### [P2-02] Market Data Client

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `get_daily_prices('MSFT', 30)` returns 30 PriceBars | ✅ | Full mock with OHLCV validation |
| Cached call makes zero API requests | ✅ | Second call verified to make 0 network hits |
| Rate limit raises `RateLimitError` | ✅ | Detects AV's `Note` and `Information` envelope patterns |

#### Strengths
- In-memory TTL cache with configurable TTL (default 1 hour)
- Smart cache design: caches the full payload, then slices by `days` — different `days` values share the same cached response (tested)
- `MissingAPIKeyError` fires before any network I/O
- `CompanyOverview` model handles AV's stringly-typed numerics with `_coerce_float` (handles `"None"`, `"-"`, `""`)
- `outputsize` switches between `compact` (≤100) and `full` (>100)

#### Tests
15 tests in [test_market_data.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_market_data.py) — covers daily prices, cache behavior, TTL expiration, rate limits (both Note and Information), company overview, unknown symbols, missing fields, and missing API key.

#### Design Doc Conformance
- `get_daily_prices(ticker, days=90)` → `list[PriceBar]` ✅
- `get_company_overview(ticker)` → `CompanyOverview` ✅
- In-memory cache with configurable TTL ✅

> [!NOTE]
> Design doc mentions an "earnings calendar" function — this is **not implemented**. Not part of the explicit acceptance criteria, but listed in the P2-02 description.

