### [P2-04] Technical Analysis Library

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| RSI of flat prices = 50.0 within tolerance | ✅ | `pytest.approx(50.0, abs=1e-9)` |
| MACD of known test vector matches to 4 decimals | ✅ | Compared against independent reference implementation |
| All raise ValueError on insufficient data | ✅ | Every function tested for this |
| 100% test coverage on this module | ✅ | Internal helpers `_to_array`, `_ema`, `_wilder_smoothed_average` all covered |

#### Strengths
- **Truly deterministic**: pure functions, no I/O, no hidden state, no LLM — exactly as the design doc mandates
- Uses Wilder's RSI (not the simpler SMA variant) — more accurate
- MACD uses SMA-seeded EMA per textbook
- Bollinger Bands use `ddof=1` (sample std) — matches pandas convention
- Sharpe ratio handles zero-volatility series (returns 0.0 instead of division by zero), FP noise tolerance
- Pydantic `MACDResult` and `BollingerResult` containers
- Functions accept both `Sequence[float]` and `np.ndarray`

#### Tests
30 tests in [test_technical.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_technical.py) — the most thorough test file in the project. Includes a **hand-rolled reference implementation** for MACD verification. Every edge case (flat, rising, falling, insufficient data, invalid params) is covered.

#### Design Doc Conformance
- `calculate_rsi(prices, period=14)` → float ✅
- `calculate_macd(prices)` → MACDResult ✅
- `calculate_bollinger(prices, period=20)` → BollingerResult ✅
- `calculate_sharpe(returns, risk_free_rate)` → float ✅
- `calculate_sma` and `calculate_ema` bonus functions ✅

