### [P2-05] Paper Trading Client

| Acceptance Criterion | Status | Notes |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| `place_paper_order('AAPL', 10, 'buy')` returns Order with `status='accepted'` | ✅ | Full request body verified |
| All calls use `paper-api.alpaca.markets`, never live endpoint | ✅ | `LiveEndpointError` raised for non-paper URLs, including empty strings |

#### Strengths
- **Critical safety guard**: `_require_paper_endpoint()` validates domain before any network I/O — cannot accidentally hit live trading
- Auth headers properly formatted for Alpaca (`APCA-API-KEY-ID`, `APCA-API-SECRET-KEY`)
- Defensive parsing: non-list responses degrade to `[]` instead of crashing
- `Order` and `Position` models use `extra="ignore"` so extra Alpaca fields don't break deserialization
- Uses raw `httpx` (not `alpaca-py`) — consistent with the rest of the data layer

#### Tests
19 tests in [test_paper_trading.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/tests/test_paper_trading.py) — covers order placement, paper endpoint validation, auth headers, invalid inputs, live endpoint rejection, positions, order history, edge cases, and missing credentials.

#### Design Doc Conformance
- `place_paper_order(ticker, qty, side)` → Order ✅
- `get_positions()` → `list[Position]` ✅
- `get_order_history(limit=50)` → `list[Order]` ✅

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `alpaca-py>=0.33.0` dependency in `pyproject.toml` is **unused**. The paper trading client uses `httpx` directly. This dependency should be removed to avoid confusion and reduce install time.

