## Cross-Cutting Observations

### What's Done Well

1. **Code quality is consistently high** — clean docstrings, consistent patterns, proper type hints, `from __future__ import annotations` everywhere
2. **Test strategy is excellent** — all HTTP clients mocked via `httpx.MockTransport`, zero flaky network dependencies, proper fixtures with autouse cleanup
3. **Error handling is thoughtful** — custom exception hierarchies, graceful degradation, no bare `except` clauses
4. **Privacy awareness** — even at this infrastructure phase, models are designed with privacy in mind (`query_hash` instead of raw queries, `portfolio_context` for generalized profiles)
5. **Safety guards** — Alpaca live endpoint blocking, API key validation before network I/O, rate limiting
6. **Integration tests separated** — `tests/integration/` has live API tests excluded from default suite via `addopts = "--ignore=tests/integration"`

### Issues & Gaps

| # | Severity | Issue | Location |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| 1 | 🟡 Medium | Health router creates new DB engine per request | [health.py:15](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/app/routers/health.py#L15) |
| 2 | 🟡 Medium | `alpaca-py` listed as dependency but never used | [pyproject.toml:22](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/pyproject.toml#L22) |
| 3 | 🟢 Low | `README.md` is a placeholder (53 bytes) | [README.md](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/README.md) |
| 4 | 🟢 Low | Docs files are all empty | `docs/API_CONTRACTS.md`, etc. |
| 5 | 🟢 Low | `paper_trading.py` router is empty and not registered in `main.py` | [paper_trading.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/app/routers/paper_trading.py) |
| 6 | 🟢 Low | Redis health check returns `"unknown"` | [health.py:31](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/app/routers/health.py#L31) |
| 7 | 🟢 Low | Earnings calendar function (mentioned in P2-02 description) not implemented | [market_data.py](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/app/tools/market_data.py) |
| 8 | 🟢 Low | Version pins use `>=` instead of exact pins | [pyproject.toml](file:///Users/mahalakshmi/fingrowth/backend/pyproject.toml) |

